{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792336986,"nonce":"SjY7Y4A5UBveAK1V24rwmI2jKYU=","title":"A fiber's error reaches the host without its payload, and runtime errors carry no source span","message":"A Rust panic in a fiber becomes Errored with no payload (krio_adapter fiber.rs:181); krio_fiber_take_error exists (fiber.rs:463-495) but neither host API exposes it (see also 4bf11db). There are no runtime source spans: HirValue.span is compile-time and InterpError has none. What happens when a host function called from JIT frames panics is unconfirmed: the runtime does not unwind through JIT frames.\n\nReported from RayDE's RayScript planning (RayDE git-bug 971d58e, latest comment); claims marked verified were checked in the code at 5c58f753, the rest come from a read-only review and their line numbers may drift.","files":null}]}